# Cursor Plugin Usage

- Plugins are advisory. `AGENTS.md`, existing project rules, approved scope, source,
  migrations, tests, and maintained documentation remain authoritative.
- Select only applicable plugins using the task matrix in
  `docs/ai/PLUGIN_OPERATING_MODEL.md`.
- Retrieve current, version-specific documentation before framework or library work.
- Use Prisma guidance for schema, migration, query, transaction, and relation work;
  retain all project migration and database-safety controls.
- Run applicable security scanners on security-sensitive diffs and use dependency
  intelligence before package changes.
- Review, deduplicate, classify, and report findings before changing code in response
  to them. Never allow automatic remediation or suppress a valid finding merely to
  obtain a green result.
- Run the applicable Cursor Team Kit review before final handoff; its Git/PR actions
  remain subject to the project's human-controlled workflow.
- No plugin may merge, force-push, rewrite history, access `dev.db`, expose secrets,
  weaken tests or CI, create credentials in Git, or expand task scope.
- Final reports must disclose plugins used, documentation topics consulted, relevant
  findings, unavailable integrations, false positives, and deferred work.
